    {
      "kind": "TextBox",
      "id": 1,
      "name": "",
      "x": 370,
      "y": 20,
      "px": 200,
      "py": 150,
      "panelOpen": false,
      "text": "BGP-Test (komplex) — Dual Stack: 10 Router, 10 autonome Systeme\n\nTier-1-Backbone: AS65001 (R1) ─── AS65002 (R2)\n                      │   ╲      ╱   │    ╲\nRegionale ISPs:  AS65003(R3) AS65004(R4) AS65005(R5)\n                    │   ╲      │    ╲      │    ╲\nKunden-AS:    R6(65006) R7(65007) R8(65008) R9(65009) R10(65010)\n\nR7 ist dual-homed: eBGP-Peers zu R3 (AS65003) und R4 (AS65004).\nBGP-Sessions: IPv4-Transport · IPv6-Präfixe via MP-BGP (RFC 4760)\nIPv4-Stub-Netze:  10.6.0.0/24 · 10.7.0.0/24 · … · 10.10.0.0/24\nIPv6-Stub-Netze:  2001:db8:6::/64 · 2001:db8:7::/64 · … · 2001:db8:a::/64\nTest-PCs: PC-R6 (an R6, AS65006) und PC-R10 (an R10, AS65010) — Dual Stack\nPing-Pfad: PC-R6 → R6 → R3 → R1 → R2 → R5 → R10 → PC-R10 (5 ASes)"
    },
